# Netflix Data Analysis Project 2025

## Project Overview

This project focuses on analyzing Netflix movies and TV shows using Python-based data science techniques. The project performs data cleaning, transformation, exploratory data analysis (EDA), and visualization to identify trends, genre popularity, voting patterns, and yearly release statistics.

The analysis helps understand user preferences, content distribution, and streaming trends on Netflix.

---

# Features

- Netflix dataset analysis
- Data preprocessing and cleaning
- Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
- Genre distribution analysis
- Genre popularity visualization
- Vote category analysis
- Year-wise release trend analysis
- Data visualization using graphs and charts

---

# Technologies Used

## Programming Language
- Python

## Libraries Used
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Jupyter Notebook

---

# Dataset Information

The project uses Netflix movie and TV show datasets containing:

- Movie titles
- Genres
- Ratings
- Popularity scores
- Release years
- Vote averages
- Vote counts

Dataset Files:

- mymoviedb.csv
- transformed_netflixdata.csv

---

# Data Analysis Performed

## 1. Data Cleaning

- Removed null values
- Handled duplicate records
- Transformed dataset columns
- Processed genre-related information

---

## 2. Genre Distribution Analysis

The project visualizes the distribution of Netflix content across different genres.

---

## 3. Genre Popularity Analysis

Analyzed which genres are most popular among Netflix users.

---

## 4. Vote Category Analysis

Classified movies based on vote categories and audience ratings.

---

## 5. Yearly Release Analysis

Analyzed the number of movies and shows released yearly.

---

